message: "If you use commonplace in your work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "commonplace: shared, durable memory for coding agents"
authors:
  - family-names: Davis
    given-names: Sean
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8991-6458"
    email: seandavi@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/seandavi/commonplace"
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
keywords:
  - ai-agents
  - agent-memory
  - mcp
  - claude-code
  - codex
  - sqlite
abstract: >-
  A small server and CLI that give coding agents (Claude Code, Codex, pi,
  omp and any MCP client) one shared memory across projects and machines.
  Memories are short, typed, versioned records in SQLite with full-text
  search, scoped to the user, a machine or a git repository. Agents get a
  one-line-per-memory index at session start and fetch full text on demand.
